Disabled 2026-08-03 by operator decision (run-all-daily / pattern-loop-analysis).

Reason: the OOS window matured 2026-08-01 and the deterministic gates now PASS
both live weight proposals, so the only thing preventing a protected
signal_registry.yaml default_weight mutation was the GPT approver's veto — and
that veto's stated reason is a verbatim echo of the prompt's own veto-criterion
sentence at backtesting/auto_apply.py:_build_prompt, and is FALSE on the data
supplied:

  STRONG_MOVE_UP  oos_hit_rate 54.47%  n=3042  ci95 [52.70, 56.23]
  VOLUME_SPIKE    oos_hit_rate 63.55%  n=214   ci95 [56.92, 69.71]

Both CIs are strictly ABOVE 50; neither straddles it. The phrase occurs nowhere
else in the repo, i.e. there was no deterministic CI-vs-no-skill screen at all.

Tracked as quant-watch ledger entry:
  manual:auto_apply_gpt_veto_reason_is_prompt_echo

Re-enable by deleting this file, but only after reviewing the deterministic CI
gate added alongside it (_ci_excludes_no_skill). Note that both proposals above
PASS that gate, so re-enabling makes them applyable on the next monthly
recompute — that should be a deliberate decision, not a side effect.
